# The Blender source and the world baked out of it.
#
# world.glb is a build artifact. `blender --background environment.blend --python recolor_land.py
# --python export_world.py` regenerates it from scratch, and at 42 MB a revision it would dominate
# the history of a repository whose next largest file is 400 KB.
#
# environment.blend is NOT an artifact — it is the source of truth for the entire world, and
# ignoring it means GIT IS NOT BACKING IT UP. That is a deliberate trade: an 18 MB binary cannot be
# diffed or merged, so every save would be a full copy and a conflict would be unresolvable. It
# needs backing up somewhere that is not this repository. Blender's own environment.blend1 is a
# single-step undo, not a backup.

world.glb
*.blend
*.blend1

# and the backup copies of it that a re-export leaves behind
*.bak
window-check/
